  "summary": "Fixes two regressions in bitcoin-cli's HTTP client introduced in PR #34342. HTTP responses with Content-Length: 0 are now recognized as complete immediately rather than reading until connection closure, and -rpcclienttimeout is restored to an idle timeout per socket wait rather than a cumulative phase deadline.",
  "problem": "In bitcoin-cli, responses with Content-Length: 0 (such as authentication error responses) bypass the fixed-length branch and wait indefinitely for the server to close the connection. Additionally, -rpcclienttimeout was converted into a hard phase deadline that ignores data transfer progress, prematurely aborting slow or large RPC responses even when data is actively being received.",
